    "First-pass metabolism and clearance of the query are not directly assessed.",
    "L3 records are for unrelated reference molecules and provide no query-specific exposure evidence."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "The query's 4-methylsulfonylphenyl-containing biaryl remains supported by multiple fasted-state human absolute F measurements in related compounds (esaxerenone 89%, BI 425809 71.6%, odanacatib 30-70%, basmisanil ~75%, pradigastat ~40-100%, imatinib ~98%), all above 20%. L3 oral AUC/Cmax records do not concern the query and do not change the decision; the only subthreshold records are low-transferability bitopertin rat micro-suspension values. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

